      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, very good point. Currently multi-site is the one that logs the consumption of messages to msgLog. Of course the aim of this change is to remove instances where other plugins log directly to msgLog, so this is an important case to consider. \n\nMoving the logging here would make sense, the only issue I see is that we lose the filter that we currently do in multi-site where we discard events generated by ourselves as well as applying other filtering.\n\nArguably it is more correct to log everything, but this would add considerable noise to the logs and complicate investigations going forward. Overall I\u0027m not a big fan of this. \n\nFiltering of the events doesn\u0027t really belong in the broker, so I\u0027m not a fan of solutions that move the filtering here.\n\nThoughts?",
